{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790286206,"nonce":"7uURN1s6NInLYqjDulezCw643aU=","title":"Lua: any metatable lookup adopts the whole string library","message":"Adoption is transitive over direct callees, and `zl_meta_of` reaches `zl_string_metatable`, which builds `zl_lib_string` with a reference to every `string.*` wrapper. So anything that looks up a metamethod on an Any adopts the string library and everything it reaches: `print` and `string.format` (through `zl_tostring`), arithmetic on Any (through `zl_arith_meta`), calls through `zl_callee`.\n\nReach from the entry, from the HIR dump (ZYNTAX_DUMP_HIR_DIR) of the L-startup-frontend build, counting functions with bodies:\n\n    print(1)              299 kept; 115 if zl_meta_of and zl_call_1 were not direct callees\n    fib.lua               303 -\u003e 127\n    any_field.lua         312 -\u003e 140\n    lambda_call.lua       304 -\u003e 128\n    mandelbrot_strip.lua  317 -\u003e 163\n\nPath for print(1): zl_lib_string \u003c- zl_string_metatable \u003c- zl_meta_of \u003c- zl_tostring \u003c- zl_print \u003c- lua$chunk.\n\nA chunk compiled by `load` pays it again per chunk: `local a, b = ... return a + b` adopts 305 functions (232 under the chunk function, via zl_arith -\u003e zl_arith_meta -\u003e zl_meta_of -\u003e zl_string_metatable; 69 under zl_chunk_add), about 10 ms of lowering per load on the Mac under load (63840a4).\n\nLevers: the string metatable's __index table built lazily through a host-resolved pointer (as $Lua$report_pending resolves the __tostring text only when an error is reported), or track C's resident library, where a module names library functions by declaration and nothing is re-adopted. Until one of them lands, the uncaught-error report was the only frontend-side edge: an empty chunk now adopts 8 functions, down from 297, but every kernel prints and so still adopts ~300.","files":null}]}